  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Prawn Cakes (tort man gung)",
  "text": "Prawn Cakes (tort man gung)\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nYield:\n\nIngredients\n\n2 coriander roots (scraped and chopped),\n\npinch of salt,\n\n3 garlic cloves (peeled),\n\n1 slice ginger,\n\nlarge pinch of ground white pepper,\n\n150g minced uncooked prawns,\n\nlarge pinch of palm sugar,\n\n1-2 tbsp soy sauce,\n\noil for deep frying.g\n\nServe with cucumber relish\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Pound the coriander roots, salt, garlic, ginger and pepper into a paste.\n\n2. Combine with the minced prawns, then slap the mixture against the side of the bowl until it becomes firm and stickier.\n\n3. Season with sugar and soy sauce. Test a little by poaching in water - it should taste salty and slightly sweet.\n\n4. Roll into 2cm balls, flatten into cakes, and deep fry in plenty of medium hot oil.",
